00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Host: Today we discuss learning from podcasts. Recognising a term is different from understanding it.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Guest: Pause after a section and explain the main idea in your own words. Write down unclear terms and revisit the source.

3
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Host: Opportunity cost means the value of the next-best alternative you give up. Studying instead of working can mean giving up wages for that hour.

4
00:00:47,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Guest: This does not make studying a bad choice. The learner may value future benefits more than today's income.

5
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Host: A short summary may omit uncertainty. Readers should be able to inspect the original passage. A confident claim is not automatically strong evidence.

6
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Guest: This conversation gives suggestions. We have not presented an experiment, so we cannot claim a measured improvement in exam scores.
